---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const articleLD = JSON.stringify({
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Article",
  "headline": "BirkyStudio vs BoldTrail (kvCORE), a Platform You Rent vs a Front Desk That Answers",
  "description": "Honest head-to-head comparison of BirkyStudio vs BoldTrail, formerly kvCORE, for real estate agents. BoldTrail publishes no prices, routes every visitor to a demo form and sells on annual contracts, with agent-reported costs around $499 per month plus a reported setup fee near $999 and ad spend billed separately. BirkyStudio answers your phone and WhatsApp 24/7 in English and Spanish, follows up automatically, and sells once instead of monthly. Real pricing, real reviews, no bias.",
  "author": {
    "@type": "Person",
    "name": "Luna Jerney",
    "url": "https://birkystudio.com"
  },
  "publisher": {
    "@type": "Organization",
    "name": "Birky Studio",
    "url": "https://birkystudio.com",
    "logo": {
      "@type": "ImageObject",
      "url": "https://birkystudio.com/images/birky-logo.jpg"
    }
  },
  "datePublished": "2026-11-10",
  "dateModified": "2026-11-10"
});

const faqLD = JSON.stringify({
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How much does BoldTrail (kvCORE) cost?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "BoldTrail publishes no prices at all. The pricing link on boldtrail.com opens a demo request form rather than a rate card, and directory listings describe it as a custom quote with pricing available upon request. Third party 2026 reviews report solo agent packages around $499 a month, setup fees somewhere near $999 one time, and ad spend billed separately, while team and brokerage quotes are reported anywhere from $1,200 to $2,500 a month. None of those figures is confirmed by the vendor, so treat them as rough and get a quote. What is published in BoldTrail's own terms is the shape of the bill: an implementation fee billed on the signing date, monthly communication and AI token fees, and MLS fees billed as incurred, with no amounts shown. Reviewers putting real numbers on the page include one paying $427.50 to $475 a month, one paying $1,600 a month plus add-ons, and one paying $1,500 a month for the managed advertising service. Many agents pay nothing directly because their brokerage covers it."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Does BoldTrail answer my phone or reply on WhatsApp?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "No. BoldTrail is an all-in-one real estate platform, not a receptionist. It bundles an IDX website, a smart CRM, lead generation, behavioural marketing automation, transaction management, back office and recruiting, and inside that stack it includes AI lead scoring, HomeSearch AI for natural language property search, and Smart Campaigns that fire on behaviour. None of it picks up a phone call and none of it holds a WhatsApp conversation. A lead that calls at 9pm reaches your voicemail. BirkyStudio answers instead: the Voice Receptionist is $550 one-time plus Vapi usage of about $30 to $50 a month and answers calls 24/7 in English and Spanish, and the WhatsApp Text Receptionist is $297 one-time."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is BoldTrail the same as kvCORE?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. Inside Real Estate rebranded its platform from kvCORE to BoldTrail in June 2024, and BoldTrail now covers the former kvCORE, BoomTown and Brokermint products. So a page or a video about kvCORE pricing, kvCORE alternatives or kvCORE login is describing the same platform, and most agents still search for it under the old name. One practical consequence is that older reviews, older comparison content and older videos all still describe BoldTrail, so a lot of what you will read about kvCORE online is really about this current product."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Do I keep my BoldTrail database if I leave my brokerage?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Usually not, and this is the part worth checking before you sign anything. When a brokerage pays for BoldTrail, the account belongs to the brokerage, and when you change firms your login typically stops working. What you can take with you depends on your independent contractor agreement and on whether you exported your contacts beforehand. The inquiries the brokerage paid to generate may reasonably belong to the brokerage, while your own past clients are a different matter, which is why agents who care about their sphere keep it somewhere they control. BirkyStudio's Notion CRM sits in your own workspace and the verified prospect list is a file you own, so nothing we build leaves with us if you stop working with us."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Does BoldTrail have a contract or a free trial?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "There is no free trial and no free plan, and the demo is a sales conversation rather than a sandbox. Annual contracts are reported as the default, with month to month rarely offered, and several reviewers describe being told they remained responsible for the rest of the term after asking to cancel. One G2 reviewer put it as holding me hostage in a contract, and another wrote that when they tried to cancel several times they were told they were stuck in a contract. BirkyStudio is contract free: no minimum term, no per-seat fee, no cancellation fee, and a 30 day money back guarantee on the build itself. Placester, Wise Agent and RealtyJuggler are all cleaner than BoldTrail on this one point as well."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is BirkyStudio a cheaper alternative to BoldTrail?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "They are different purchases, so the honest answer is yes for the front desk and no for the platform. If what you need is an IDX website, a team lead routing engine, back office commissions and a recruiting module, BoldTrail does things BirkyStudio does not do at any price, and if your brokerage gives it to you at no direct cost then the value question is over. If what you need is somebody to answer the phone and the WhatsApp at 9pm in two languages, BirkyStudio is dramatically cheaper: The Base Agent is $1,297 one-time with the Notion CRM included, and with optional care at $97 a month that is about $2,461 in year one and about $4,789 over three years, against about $5,988 in year one and about $17,964 over three years at the reported BoldTrail rate of $499 a month, before the reported setup fee and add-ons."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Does BoldTrail include IDX and lead generation?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "It includes both, and this is where BoldTrail is genuinely strong. IDX consumer websites are included in the base subscription with no separate IDX fee, which is better than most of its competitors who charge for IDX on top. Lead generation is available as an option rather than being mandatory, drawing from Google, Facebook and portal capture, and managed advertising packages are also sold. The catch is that lead generation is where the money and the complaints both live. Third party and reviewer reported ad spend runs separately from the platform fee, one reviewer paid $1,500 a month for managed advertising, and the most repeated criticism across Capterra, G2 and Software Advice is that the leads do not match the service area or the volume promised. BirkyStudio does not sell portal leads at all; its Verified Prospect List is a one-time file of verified, enriched, scored prospects you own."
      }
    }
  ]
});
---

<BaseLayout
  title="BirkyStudio vs BoldTrail kvCORE (2026)"
