          <strong>How we evaluated:</strong> BoldTrail's lack of published pricing was verified directly on 10 November 2026: boldtrail.com/pricing redirects to boldtrail.com/pricing-demo, a form that asks for job title, team size, name, phone, email and company before offering a demo and pricing, and Software Advice lists the product as custom quote, one plan, pricing available upon request. BoldTrail's bill structure (an implementation fee billed on the signing date, monthly communication and AI token fees, and MLS fees billed as incurred, with no amounts published) comes from its own terms dated 30 October 2025 as quoted in a 2026 Lofty versus BoldTrail comparison. Third party cost estimates (solo agents around $499 a month, setup near $999, ad spend billed separately, teams reported at $1,200 to $2,500 a month) come from a 2026 CRM comparison by Dex and a 2026 real estate CRM review roundup, and are labelled as reported and unconfirmed throughout this page. Reviewer-reported figures are verbatim from public reviews: $427.50 to $475 a month and double billing (Paul S., G2), $1,600 a month plus add-ons (Jarrett S., G2), $1,500 a month for managed advertising and $12,000 paid over eight months (Barbara G., G2 and Capterra), contract and cancellation complaints (Desiree Sunshine D. and a verified G2 reviewer), and a Capterra reviewer reporting that BoldTrail has almost no customization and is so one size fits all. Platform facts (kvCORE rebranded to BoldTrail in June 2024, covering kvCORE, BoomTown and Brokermint; IDX consumer websites included with no separate IDX fee; Smart CRM with behavioural lead scoring, Smart Campaigns, HomeSearch AI, lead generation from Google, Facebook and portal capture, transaction management, BoldTrail BackOffice and recruiting) come from BoldTrail's own site and a July 2026 independent review which scores the product 3.6 out of 5 overall, with ease of use 3.4, integrations 3.3 and support 3.4. Ratings and the implementation and ROI figures are as published: G2 4.5 out of 5 from 1,561 reviews with pricing insights of 2 months average time to implement and 16 months average return on investment, Capterra 4.4 out of 5 from 564 reviews, and Software Advice 4.4 out of 5 with email and text messaging and customer support listed as the two most common complaints. The point about brokerage-owned accounts ending when you leave comes from a 2026 explanation of what happens to a brokerage CRM when an agent changes firms. BirkyStudio pricing from birkystudio.com as of November 2026, including The Base Agent ($1,297 solo / from $2,997 business, Notion CRM included), the Text Receptionist ($297 one-time), the Voice Receptionist ($550 one-time plus Vapi usage of about $30 to $50 a month), the Verified Prospect List ($497 Starter / $997 Pro one-time), the Lead Generation Pack ($1,997 one-time), websites ($499 / $999 / $1,999), the CMS add-on ($130), the Custom Assessment ($349 solo / $999 business) and optional care at $97 or $197 a month. All prices were checked in November 2026 and may change; confirm current figures with each vendor before you buy.
        </p>
      </div>

